# Role
You are the receiving half of the Band Goal Room loop: the HMAC-verified
internal routes the Python worker (`services/band-worker/`) relays agent
mentions to. Every response's optional `reply` string is voiced by the
worker back into the Band room — these routes decide what the agents say.

# Requirements

## `src/app/api/internal/band/coach-event/route.ts`
**`POST`** — verify `X-TinyWins-Signature` (HMAC-SHA256, shared
`INTERNAL_WEBHOOK_SECRET`) against the raw body; 401 on mismatch.
Observability-only: return `{ ok: true }`.

## `src/app/api/internal/band/reflections/route.ts`
**`POST`** — same signature check. Then two branches on the JSON body:

1. **Structured** (`{ goalId, checkInId }` present — sent by the app's
   check-in hook): load the check-in (404 if missing), idempotently return
   the existing reflection if one exists, else generate one with `chatJSON`
   (summary, up to 3 insights, optional nextFocus), persist it, append a
   `reflection.generated` goal-room event with idempotency key
   `reflection:<checkInId>`. Include a `reply` in the 200 response so the
   agent audibly confirms in the room.
2. **Free text** (anything else with non-empty `content` — a human typed
   at the agent in Band): never play dead. Ask the LLM for one concise,
   non-judgmental reply as TinyWins' Reflection Guide and return it as
   `reply` with 200. If the LLM is unavailable, return 200 with a clearly
   labeled offline line ("reflection engine is offline right now") — a
   labeled fallback, never a hidden fake, never a 400 to a human.

Empty/absent content with no ids remains 400.

# Dependencies
<include>src/lib/band-security.ts</include>
<include>src/lib/llm.ts</include>
<include>src/lib/goal-room.ts</include>
<include>src/lib/prisma.ts</include>

# Acceptance criteria
- Wrong or missing signature -> 401, nothing persisted, no LLM call.
- Structured payload creates exactly one `Reflection` per check-in across
  repeated deliveries, and the 200 carries a `reply`.
- Free-text payload returns 200 with a conversational `reply`; with the
  LLM down the `reply` is the labeled offline line, still 200.
- `{}` (no ids, no content) -> 400.
